WEBVTT

00:00:39.720 --> 00:00:41.290
It's a beast-lord!

00:01:05.390 --> 00:01:11.300
New Life

00:01:12.940 --> 00:01:18.200
The seasons had changed, and one sunny spring afternoon,

00:01:19.000 --> 00:01:22.640
a carriage was brought to Kazalm.

00:01:27.450 --> 00:01:28.960
It's here, it's here, it's here!

00:01:29.550 --> 00:01:32.580
Wow, it's so big.

00:01:32.580 --> 00:01:38.220
After all, it's a fully grown wild beast-lord.

00:01:38.950 --> 00:01:41.690
Hear that?  It's a wild beast-lord.

00:01:41.690 --> 00:01:46.330
That reminds me of how the little girl was so happy about seeing one in the mountains.

00:01:46.330 --> 00:01:48.180
It brings back memories.

00:01:50.070 --> 00:01:51.500
What's up, Mokku?

00:01:52.050 --> 00:01:54.140
It's a beast-lord's feather.

00:01:54.140 --> 00:01:57.410
Wow.  It's shiny.

00:01:57.410 --> 00:01:59.410
I'm gonna give it to Erin-chan.

00:01:59.410 --> 00:02:00.920
I'm sure she'll be happy.

00:02:00.920 --> 00:02:02.490
Hey, give that to me!

00:02:02.490 --> 00:02:03.700
I'll give it to her.

00:02:03.700 --> 00:02:05.540
No!  I found it!

00:02:05.540 --> 00:02:06.550
Don't be stingy!

00:02:06.550 --> 00:02:07.280
No!

00:02:07.330 --> 00:02:07.840
Give it to me!

00:02:07.850 --> 00:02:08.400
No!

00:02:08.400 --> 00:02:08.840
Give it to me!

00:02:08.840 --> 00:02:09.420
No!

00:02:14.150 --> 00:02:17.630
But why did it get injured?

00:02:17.630 --> 00:02:22.390
It's a parent that came back while some guys were taking its baby away.

00:02:25.130 --> 00:02:30.580
They instinctively blew the mute whistle, so it froze in the air, and then crashed into a cliff.

00:02:32.610 --> 00:02:35.340
They couldn't neglect the injured beast-lord,

00:02:35.340 --> 00:02:38.880
so they sent the captured baby to Lazal's Beast-Lord Care Center.

00:02:38.880 --> 00:02:42.550
The injured beast-lord was brought here.

00:02:43.160 --> 00:02:47.990
I see.  So that's a mommy that tried to save her baby.

00:02:47.990 --> 00:02:50.890
Not a mommy, but a daddy.

00:02:51.400 --> 00:02:53.700
That beast-lord's a male I heard.

00:02:53.700 --> 00:02:56.860
We'll be calling him Eku.

00:02:56.860 --> 00:02:57.820
"Eku?"

00:02:58.600 --> 00:03:01.420
It means "male" in the old language.

00:03:04.150 --> 00:03:05.610
Eku...

00:03:05.610 --> 00:03:06.440
Erin.

00:03:07.690 --> 00:03:08.640
Y-Yes?

00:03:09.500 --> 00:03:11.770
The Reverend of the Teachers is calling for you.

00:03:13.510 --> 00:03:15.980
The beast-lord has arrived.

00:03:15.980 --> 00:03:24.540
Good grief.  It looks like the people at the capital think they can give us all the beast-lord-related problems.

00:03:24.540 --> 00:03:30.720
You're right.  Reading the report from Lazal, Eku's condition isn't great.

00:03:30.720 --> 00:03:33.850
Treating him will be very difficult.

00:03:35.340 --> 00:03:36.200
Come in.

00:03:37.560 --> 00:03:39.470
I brought Erin.

00:03:39.470 --> 00:03:40.430
Excuse me.

00:03:45.050 --> 00:03:46.560
I've been waiting for you.

00:03:47.800 --> 00:03:48.570
Erin.

00:03:50.870 --> 00:03:56.980
Even if you treat Eku while he's frozen with the mute whistle, he goes wild as soon as he wakes up.

00:03:57.370 --> 00:03:59.740
So the wounds open right up.

00:04:02.630 --> 00:04:04.870
Just like Lilan in the past.

00:04:04.870 --> 00:04:05.760
You're right.

00:04:08.890 --> 00:04:10.960
Looks like he's awake.

00:04:18.500 --> 00:04:20.090
Don't!  Stop that!

00:04:20.730 --> 00:04:24.550
Eku had been injured right after the mute whistle was blown.

00:04:25.510 --> 00:04:32.140
The sound of the whistle and the injury have definitely been linked in his mind, causing him to panic.

00:04:32.140 --> 00:04:34.520
So I have a favor to ask you.

00:04:35.250 --> 00:04:38.500
Can you calm Eku down with your harp?

00:04:38.500 --> 00:04:42.890
Unlike Lilan's case, Eku is already fully grown.

00:04:42.890 --> 00:04:48.010
It might not work the same way, but it's worth a try, right?

00:04:50.500 --> 00:04:53.390
Okay.  I'll give it a try.

00:05:03.590 --> 00:05:05.700
The shed's going to break down!

00:05:12.350 --> 00:05:14.180
Do you think you can do this?

00:05:15.540 --> 00:05:16.810
I don't know.

00:05:17.350 --> 00:05:21.720
But I don't think he'd listen to the harp even if I played it now.

00:05:21.720 --> 00:05:23.760
He's too excited.

00:05:24.850 --> 00:05:29.490
Give me a day please.  I'll spend the night here.

00:05:43.330 --> 00:05:47.610
Erin's going to be looking after that wild beast-lord?

00:05:47.610 --> 00:05:53.730
Yeah.  She's all up to spending the night with him and ran out of the dorm with a blanket.

00:05:54.340 --> 00:05:56.350
That's beast-lord gung-ho for you.

00:06:06.400 --> 00:06:08.740
The little girl looks busy.

00:06:08.740 --> 00:06:10.060
Yeah.

00:06:13.040 --> 00:06:14.410
It's Lilan.

00:06:15.650 --> 00:06:16.890
She's coming toward us!

00:06:16.890 --> 00:06:17.950
You stop her, Mokku!

00:06:17.950 --> 00:06:19.330
You stop her!

00:06:19.330 --> 00:06:20.380
You!

00:06:20.380 --> 00:06:21.210
No, you!

00:06:21.210 --> 00:06:22.000
You!

00:06:22.000 --> 00:06:22.920
No, you!

00:06:46.360 --> 00:06:50.760
It's fine.  There's nothing to be scared of here.

00:06:54.370 --> 00:06:57.180
You're fine.  You can relax.

00:07:36.840 --> 00:07:39.040
Have you calmed down, Eku?

00:09:08.170 --> 00:09:11.550
I'm very glad that I put Eku in your charge.

00:09:12.050 --> 00:09:17.640
Can you communicate with all wild beast-lords with that harp?

00:09:20.600 --> 00:09:21.600
Probably.

00:09:24.980 --> 00:09:26.190
<i>"Crime?" </i>

00:09:28.310 --> 00:09:32.490
<i>Mother said "crime" then, too.</i>

00:09:32.490 --> 00:09:35.990
<i>Was she referring to communicating with Touda?</i>

00:09:35.990 --> 00:09:40.080
<i>Yes.  And it's the same with communicating with beast-lords.</i>

00:09:41.790 --> 00:09:44.580
<i>Why exactly is it a crime?</i>

00:09:48.630 --> 00:09:50.040
Is something wrong, Erin?

00:09:50.880 --> 00:09:53.760
Nothing.  But, um...

00:09:57.150 --> 00:09:58.510
Esal-sensei.

00:09:59.220 --> 00:10:01.510
There's something I want you to hear me out over.

00:10:07.350 --> 00:10:14.030
Erin told Esal the story she was told by Nason, the man of the Mist People.

00:10:15.110 --> 00:10:19.840
The old story pertaining to the Founding Queen Je and to the beast-lords.

00:10:20.240 --> 00:10:24.450
The history of war, despair, and destruction.

00:10:26.040 --> 00:10:29.330
I see.  I understand the story.

00:10:30.380 --> 00:10:35.130
That there should be such a history underneath the foundation of this country and the symbol of beast-lord...

00:10:38.720 --> 00:10:44.470
I, too, met a man of the Mist People before.

00:10:45.560 --> 00:10:47.730
It was deep in the mountains.

00:10:48.200 --> 00:10:52.330
This must be the catastrophe he was talking about.

00:11:15.930 --> 00:11:17.550
Green eyes!

00:11:17.830 --> 00:11:21.030
Stop looking for wild beast-lords.

00:11:22.550 --> 00:11:24.350
Why?!

00:11:24.350 --> 00:11:29.600
A wild beast-lord that falls into human hands will be controlled by codes from that moment on.

00:11:29.600 --> 00:11:36.750
When a wise researcher such as yourself, who's in the position of raising the Queen's beast-lords,

00:11:37.150 --> 00:11:42.740
sees a wild beast-lord, you'll only be creating a seed for a catastrophe.

00:11:42.740 --> 00:11:43.950
"Catastrophe?"

00:11:44.530 --> 00:11:50.540
It would be a seed of catastrophe that you couldn't possibly repent enough for later.

00:11:52.670 --> 00:11:54.810
Do you want to take that step?

00:12:12.310 --> 00:12:14.280
I'm finally able to understand.

00:12:14.980 --> 00:12:22.780
Mist People banned the technique to control Touda and beast-lords so that the same mistake will never happen again.

00:12:24.240 --> 00:12:31.930
The Mist People told me to stop communicating with beast-lords or flying on them.

00:12:32.870 --> 00:12:37.550
But I just can't make myself agree that it's the right thing to do.

00:12:39.050 --> 00:12:41.840
I understand what they are worried about.

00:12:41.840 --> 00:12:50.770
But I think it's strange to tie them down by the codes humans have made because they can be the cause of catastrophe.

00:12:51.980 --> 00:12:57.540
I think it's humans that should keep an eye on themselves to ensure the same mistake doesn't happen.

00:13:13.600 --> 00:13:16.140
You really are amazing.

00:13:16.810 --> 00:13:18.650
Tomura-senpai.

00:13:18.650 --> 00:13:23.550
I never thought you'd tame a wild beast-lord.

00:13:23.560 --> 00:13:25.990
It's because this is a very simple sound.

00:13:26.550 --> 00:13:31.450
Actually by using it, it's more like being able to mimic a greeting in another language.

00:13:31.970 --> 00:13:34.060
Greeting, huh?

00:13:34.060 --> 00:13:35.340
Yes.

00:13:35.350 --> 00:13:41.440
When Lilan gets too close to other beast-lords, she often makes a similar sound.

00:13:42.230 --> 00:13:47.180
I think it's a sound made between beast-lords to communicate that they mean no hostility.

00:13:52.750 --> 00:14:04.130
By communicating verbally, this might be a sign that they actually live in packs.

00:14:04.150 --> 00:14:05.660
You're right.

00:14:05.660 --> 00:14:10.320
If they live alone, then there's no need for them to be able to communicate.

00:14:11.160 --> 00:14:15.570
Beast-lords are still full of mysteries.

00:14:21.230 --> 00:14:33.490
Ever since he answered the harp's tune, Eku stopped going wild, ate the food Erin brought, and became better by the day.

00:14:34.040 --> 00:14:43.460
The treatments were completed as he slept from sleeping pills mixed in the food, so the mute whistle wasn't needed.

00:14:44.050 --> 00:14:48.140
From the looks of this, we can let him out in the field by tomorrow.

00:14:48.140 --> 00:14:49.390
You're right.

00:14:49.390 --> 00:14:53.870
Once he regains the power to fly, he should be able to return to the wild.

00:14:54.890 --> 00:14:56.350
"To the wild?!"

00:14:56.350 --> 00:14:58.390
We're not going to turn him in to Lazal?

00:14:59.000 --> 00:15:06.170
No.  Eku was captured accidentally.  He wasn't offered to the Queen.

00:15:15.090 --> 00:15:18.360
Eku can return to the wild.

00:15:25.420 --> 00:15:26.570
I'm sorry.

00:15:26.960 --> 00:15:30.550
It's been a while, so let me make you really pretty.

00:15:48.150 --> 00:15:49.740
Where are you going, Lilan?

00:15:57.620 --> 00:15:59.710
Is Eku's scent interesting to you?

00:16:01.000 --> 00:16:03.670
You'll get to see him when you go out to the field tomorrow.

00:16:04.400 --> 00:16:06.640
If you meet him, be friends with him, okay?

00:16:11.020 --> 00:16:12.090
Hey.

00:16:12.890 --> 00:16:14.790
What's wrong with the color of that fur?

00:16:19.300 --> 00:16:20.980
This is...

00:16:23.920 --> 00:16:25.400
I don't see anything.

00:16:25.970 --> 00:16:28.630
It's not talked about in any book.

00:16:29.420 --> 00:16:35.090
I've worked with beast-lords for a long time, but I've never seen the color of the fur change.

00:16:35.900 --> 00:16:37.350
I see.

00:16:37.870 --> 00:16:41.080
Is there any difference in the amount of food she eats or the content of the feces?

00:16:41.750 --> 00:16:44.170
No, there aren't any problems.

00:16:44.170 --> 00:16:47.050
In fact, it looks better than usual.

00:16:47.050 --> 00:16:49.800
So I don't think she's sick.

00:16:50.630 --> 00:16:54.320
She also seems to be very interested in Eku's scent.

00:16:54.600 --> 00:16:56.110
Really?

00:16:56.110 --> 00:17:00.310
But I guess that means they'll be able to get along even if Eku's out there.

00:17:00.880 --> 00:17:06.040
Yes.  Lilan didn't show any hostility, so I think it'll be fine.

00:17:06.650 --> 00:17:11.150
I'll research about that fur color myself.

00:17:11.150 --> 00:17:15.570
Let me know if anything else comes up that catches your attention.

00:17:15.590 --> 00:17:16.470
I will.

00:17:22.550 --> 00:17:23.800
Here he comes.

00:17:24.410 --> 00:17:26.170
Finally coming out into the sun.

00:17:29.550 --> 00:17:31.800
His wings are so beautiful.

00:17:31.800 --> 00:17:34.180
So that's what wild ones look like.

00:17:34.180 --> 00:17:36.610
It's similar to Lilan.

00:17:52.570 --> 00:17:55.030
All right you, get out there and have fun.

00:18:05.690 --> 00:18:06.390
It's Lilan.

00:18:37.310 --> 00:18:39.310
Looks like they're getting along.

00:18:39.320 --> 00:18:42.410
Their first contact seems to be a success.

00:18:44.210 --> 00:18:45.350
This is great.

00:18:45.910 --> 00:18:50.350
It might be for a short time, but Lilan now has a good friend.

00:18:50.900 --> 00:18:53.270
Yes.  I'm very glad.

00:18:54.830 --> 00:18:57.880
This is what wild beast-lords look like.

00:18:59.760 --> 00:19:05.740
How they should appear without being influenced by humans.

00:19:09.070 --> 00:19:12.960
They're like turtledoves.  What a wonderful sight.

00:19:28.890 --> 00:19:29.960
Lilan?

00:19:32.670 --> 00:19:34.920
That's a sound we've never heard before.

00:19:35.770 --> 00:19:37.620
What is that cry?

00:19:39.340 --> 00:19:41.610
What's going on?

00:19:44.280 --> 00:19:45.260
Lilan!

00:21:35.590 --> 00:21:39.960
What are they doing?

00:21:40.420 --> 00:21:42.940
Could they be mating?

00:21:43.540 --> 00:21:50.180
It has to be.  Lilan and Eku are working to create a new life.

00:21:51.250 --> 00:21:57.770
It was very beautiful view, wrapped in an aura of divinity.

00:21:57.770 --> 00:22:09.570
It surpassed any trivial worries humans could possibly have, as Eku and Lilan tried to create a new life.

00:22:11.450 --> 00:22:14.540
The power of the wild that's not bound by codes...

00:22:15.580 --> 00:22:25.220
Seeing that power and beauty, Erin could only observe.

00:24:02.070 --> 00:24:05.200
Erin, we're finally graduating, aren't we?

00:24:05.200 --> 00:24:09.540
And Lilan-chan, who was a baby, is
about to become a mother, too.

00:24:09.540 --> 00:24:14.500
Yet your mind still becomes completely occupied when it comes to beast-lords!

00:24:14.500 --> 00:24:17.420
It's been four years of nonstop excitement.

00:24:17.420 --> 00:24:22.260
I think I'm forgetting something
important, but what was it?

00:24:22.260 --> 00:24:25.000
Kemono no Souja Erin.  Graduation Trial.

00:24:25.000 --> 00:26:00.020
Graduation Trial
